WEBVTT - The Evilginx Trap: Reverse Proxy Session Hijack (English)

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Late at night, an IT administrator received an urgent message: 'Your login session is about to expire.'

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:50.000
The page looked identical to his company’s login screen. Attackers set up a digital two-way mirror between him and the real site.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:15.000
This technique is called a reverse proxy. When you type your password, the fake page passes your information to the real website.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:35.000
The real site logs you in—but the attacker sitting in the middle steals your digital session pass.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:50.000
TraceXMail discovered that the link didn't point to the company’s portal at all, but to a hidden relay server.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:15.000
TraceXMail spotted the trick by measuring speed. An email passing directly moves in milliseconds.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Here, there was an unnatural delay of over 400 milliseconds—proof of an invisible detour through an encrypted tunnel.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:55.000
TraceXMail unmasked the hidden detour before the engineer could log in.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:20.000
By looking at the physical transmission route rather than just web page appearance, TraceXMail stopped the attack.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:45.000
The administrator's access stayed safe, company cloud systems remained secure, and the incident was closed without a breach.
